btrfs: complete a checksum-free read or write where it finished

Every data read on btrfs is handed to the end-io workqueue before its
completion runs, so that checksums can be verified and a bad sector
repaired from another copy. A read from an inode with no checksums — every
file on a nodatacow volume — has neither to do, and the worker wakeup it
still pays is most of the cost of a cached 4 KiB read: fio at queue depth 1
read at 39k a second on btrfs and 464k on ext4 on the same kernel, with the
device completing inside the submit in both cases.

So a clean data read with no checksums to check completes on the CPU that
found it, as ext4's do. Reads with checksums, reads that failed, and repair
bios keep the workqueue; metadata reads keep it too, for now, since their
completion validates the tree block.

6.18 sends every completion, writes included, through the workqueue,
and asserts task context in the completion itself — a checksum computed
alongside a write is waited for there. A read or write found by the
submitter's own poll is in task context and, without checksums, has
nothing to wait for; it completes in place. One delivered by interrupt
keeps the worker. fio direct writes at queue depth 1 on 6.18: 32k a second
through the worker.

--- a/fs/btrfs/bio.c
+++ b/fs/btrfs/bio.c
@@ -351,6 +351,29 @@
 	if (bio->bi_status)
 		btrfs_log_dev_io_error(bio, dev);
 
+	/*
+	 * The workqueue exists to verify checksums, to wait for a checksum
+	 * being computed alongside a write, and to repair. A data read that
+	 * returned cleanly from an inode with no checksums has none of those
+	 * to do, and neither has a clean write with no checksum in flight.
+	 * Completing them here saves the worker wakeup, which was most of
+	 * the cost of a cached 4 KiB read and of a small direct write.
+	 * Completion must run in task context, which a request found by the
+	 * submitter's own poll is; one delivered by interrupt keeps the
+	 * worker. Repair bios keep their path (the repair code checks them,
+	 * not their inode), and so do zone appends, which record their
+	 * physical address first.
+	 */
+	if (!bio->bi_status && in_task() &&
+	    bio->bi_pool != &btrfs_repair_bioset &&
+	    ((bio_op(bio) == REQ_OP_READ && is_data_bbio(bbio) &&
+	      !bbio->csum) ||
+	     (bio_op(bio) == REQ_OP_WRITE && !bbio->async_csum &&
+	      !bio_is_zone_append(bio)))) {
+		btrfs_bio_end_io(bbio, BLK_STS_OK);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	INIT_WORK(&bbio->end_io_work, simple_end_io_work);
 	queue_work(btrfs_end_io_wq(fs_info, bio), &bbio->end_io_work);
 }
